error: Multiple generic publishers detected without explicit message type constraints, which would create conflicting trait implementations.

       Tip: When using multiple generic publishers, you must specify explicit message types to avoid conflicts:

       Instead of:
         struct MyStruct<A, B>
         where
             A: Publisher,
             B: Publisher,

       Use one of these approaches:
         1. Explicit message type constraints:
            struct MyStruct<A, B>
            where
                A: Publisher<InputMessage = i32, OutputMessage = String>,
                B: Publisher<InputMessage = bool, OutputMessage = f64>,

         2. Use #[publisher] attributes with explicit types:
            struct MyStruct {
                #[publisher(i32, String)] field_a: A,
                #[publisher(bool, f64)] field_b: B,
            }
